      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "The row echelon form matrix $M$ is given below. What are the pivot columns of $M?$\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $M$ has $3$ pivots in the $2$nd, $3$rd, and $5$th columns:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
